@startuml
' US-14 — Look at a picture closely.
' Sequence — the picture at its own pixels, the zoom, and the hand
' Sources: ../../../analysis/stories.md (US-14), ../../../specification/03-features.md (F-19, F-20, F-21, F-28)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333
autonumber

actor Reader
participant "The picture's page" as PAGE
participant "The stage" as STAGE
participant "The image" as IMG
participant "The tools" as BAR

Reader -> PAGE : opens the file
activate PAGE
PAGE -> IMG : the picture
activate IMG
IMG -> PAGE : its own size — 1536 by 1024
deactivate IMG
PAGE -> STAGE : the picture is drawn at its own pixels (F-19)
deactivate PAGE
PAGE -> Reader : the picture, sharp

Reader -> BAR : zooms in
activate BAR
BAR -> STAGE : zoom about the pointer (F-20)
activate STAGE
STAGE -> IMG : the scale changes, and what is\nunder the pointer stays under it
deactivate STAGE
deactivate BAR

Reader -> STAGE : drags the picture
activate STAGE
STAGE -> STAGE : the picture moves with the pointer (F-21)
deactivate STAGE

Reader -> BAR : fits it, or puts it back to 1:1
activate BAR
BAR -> STAGE : the scale changes
deactivate BAR

Reader -> PAGE : clicks a picture in a note
activate PAGE
PAGE -> PAGE : the picture opens in this view,\nin a tab of the window above (F-28)
deactivate PAGE

note right
  F-19: a picture is shown at its own pixels
  and is not shrunk to fit the window: a
  shrunk picture is a soft one.

  F-20: the zoom is about the pointer.

  F-21: a picture bigger than the window is
  moved with the hand.
end note
@enduml
